it was just days after Christmas last  year Keith bromyard was told he had  inoperable pancreatic cancer  six weeks later he died without ever  receiving treatment  it took three months from Keith's first  symptoms to his first CT scan delays his  daughter Rebecca believes that reduced  his chances of surviving if it was  picked up sooner would we be in a  different position would we would we be  sat here talking about my dad's survival  rather than my dad's death and so it  does leave a very bitter taste that he  had to wait such a long time to get any  kind of appointment really okay if you  can just bear with me a moment I'm just  going to get his details up on the  screen for the past year Dr trisker and  his team have been taking part in a  trial giving gp's direct access to  diagnostic scams a program Now set to be  rolled out across the country it means  tens of thousands of cancers each year  might be detected earlier leading to  patients getting potentially life-saving  treatment it's something that is really  important to get patients accurate  treatment earlier save lives and it  brings us into line with many of our  world Partners so the UK is something of  an outlier in that GPS don't have access  to direct Imaging tests  GPS and Cancer Care are among the  services facing possible funding Cuts  next year because of a seven billion  pound shortfall in the NHS budget caused  by inflationary pressures but the health  secretary has indicated the NHS will  receive more funding and the  Chancellor's Autumn statements the  chancellor needs to balance through his  fiscal statement The Wider economic  picture built of course within the  Health and Social care sector as with so  many others there are pressures from  inflation Steve Barkley says supporting  the NHS Workforce is a priority but  faced with one of the toughest Winters  in NHS history and with unions across  the sector considering strike action the  demands for extra NHS funding will not  end tomorrow  artist Joshy Sky News
 

